        "description": "Learn the four menstrual cycle phases, what FSH, LH, estrogen, and progesterone do, how long a normal cycle lasts, and when cycle length deserves a clinician visit.",
        "intro": "The menstrual cycle has four phases: menstruation, the follicular phase, ovulation, and the luteal phase. On a typical 28-day cycle, bleeding covers roughly days 1 to 5, the follicular phase runs from day 1 until ovulation around day 14, and the luteal phase fills the final two weeks. Real cycles range from about 21 to 35 days in adults, and that whole spread is normal. This guide walks through each phase, the hormones behind it, and when cycle length deserves a closer look.",
