        "description": "Learn the common signs of ovulation, which ones appear early enough to help you time sex, and which ones only confirm that an egg has already been released.",
        "intro": "The most common signs of ovulation are cervical mucus that turns clear and stretchy, a mild one-sided ache in the lower belly, light spotting, breast tenderness, a higher sex drive, and a small rise in resting body temperature after the egg is released. Some of these signs arrive early enough to help you time sex, while others only confirm ovulation once it has passed. This guide sorts them into those two groups, so you know which ones to act on. And if you notice none of them, you are in good company: plenty of people ovulate every cycle without feeling a thing.",
